<section class="hero" id="home"><div class="wrap hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">An independent student technology zine · Issue 01</div><h1 class="headline">THE HUMAN<br/>IN THE <em>LOOP.</em></h1><p class="lead">AI is changing the way we work. But what happens to the people behind the job?</p><div class="hero-badges"><span class="pill">TECH + WORK</span><span class="pill">PEOPLE FIRST</span><span class="pill">FINANCE + GLOBAL BUSINESS</span></div><a class="cta" href="#contents">Explore the issue <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div aria-label="Graphic magazine cover with the words Human Intelligence, Artificial Intelligence, and Work Together" class="poster" role="img"><span class="poster-small">ZINE / VOL. 01 / 2026</span><div class="poster-center">HUMAN<br/><span>≠</span> MACHINE<br/><span>+</span> TOGETHER.</div><span class="poster-bottom">THE FUTURE IS A TEAM SPORT ★</span></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="editors"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><span class="section-label">From the Editors</span><h2>Technology moves fast. People matter.</h2><div class="quote-card">"The question isn't just what AI can do. It's what we choose to do with it."</div></div><div><p>Artificial intelligence is entering workplaces everywhere, changing how tasks are completed and how people prepare for their careers. Some changes are exciting. Others raise difficult questions about job security, responsibility, and trust.</p><p>In this issue, we look at work through a people-first lens. We explore what technology does well, where it falls short, and why creativity, judgment, and human relationships still count.</p><p>Our features explore two connected careers: financial analysts, who interpret money and investment data, and international business analysts, who help companies make decisions across borders. In both fields, AI can accelerate research—but responsible choices still require people.</p><p><strong>— The Editorial Team</strong></p><!-- EDIT WITH YOUR GROUP: Customize this joint editors' letter to mention all of your teammates' fields. --></div></div></section>
